<!--
  ZA.Saga v3.0.0 - intentional API breaks for the major version bump.

  Eight member removals, each across three TFMs. All of them are the same change:
  ISagaBuilder carried one boolean per backend, IsEfCoreBackend and IsRedisBackend,
  with a settable mirror on ISagaBuilderMutable and a SetXxxBackend helper for each.
  That enumerated the backends this package knew about, so shipping a new store meant
  editing the core interface and copying the mutual-exclusion check again.

  They are replaced by a single HasDurableStore flag and SetDurableStore helper. What
  the composition path needs to know is whether a durable store is present at all;
  which one it is comes from SagaStoreRegistrar, which the backend installs itself.

  A backend that genuinely needs to identify another backend - the Redis outbox bridge
  enlists into the Redis store's MULTI/EXEC - now looks for that backend's own
  registration in the service collection instead.

  This break is loud: a custom ISagaBuilder fails to compile with a named missing
  member. The other break in v3.0.0, conflict detection moving from exception type
  names to ISagaConcurrencyConflict, is silent at runtime and is the one worth reading
  the release notes for.

  Each entry sets IsBaselineSuppression=true because the api-compat workflow compares
  the newly built package against the latest released baseline.
-->
<Suppressions>

  <!-- CP0002: get_IsEfCoreBackend -->
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:ZeroAlloc.Saga.ISagaBuilder.get_IsEfCoreBackend</Target>
    <Left>lib/net8.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net8.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
    <Justification>Replaced by HasDurableStore. The flag named one backend while meaning 'a durable store is configured'; a per-backend boolean had to be added to this interface for every new store.</Justification>
  </Suppression>
